--
N5008 [class.base.init]/9.1, [class.default.ctor]/4: a virtual base not
named in the most derived class's mem-initializer-list is
default-initialized, which applies its default member initializers.  The
front end constructs virtual bases only when they are non-POD (cpp_is_pod
ignores NSDMIs), so the members of a POD virtual base with NSDMIs were
nondeterministic (bin53).  full_member_initialization now applies them to
the virtual base's members in the `@most_derived' block.  Found from
libstdc++'s basic_ios (`_M_num_put = nullptr' etc.), a virtual base of
basic_ostream (cpp11_libstdcxx_header_drops/test_ostream_int.desc).  g++
13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
